<title>USA: Muni bond sales total $1.2 bln for week of Jan 27.</title>
<headline>Muni bond sales total $1.2 bln for week of Jan 27.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scheduled competitive and negotiated municipal bond sales for the week of Jan 27 are expected to total $1.2 billion in 72 offerings, according to Reuters Municipal Bond Information Group.</p>
<p>Competitive sales total $491 million in 51 sales. The largest is a $50 million West Virginia Housing Development Fund issue on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Negotiated sales total $696 million in 21 offerings. The largest is a $134 million Suffolk County Industrial Development Authority, N.Y., deal through Smith Barney Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Information Group, 212-859-1826</p>
</text>
